cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the technical paper and repository if you use this result or certificate. See CONTRIBUTORS.md for the research lineage."
title: "Parent-aware lower bound and recentered-core sharpening for packing 17 unit squares in a square"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Mira"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-20
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mira-acc/17squares"
url: "https://github.com/Mira-acc/17squares/blob/main/paper/17squares-lower-bound.pdf"
abstract: >-
  Exact computer-assisted proof that the minimum containing-square side length
  for 17 pairwise interior-disjoint unit squares satisfies
  s(17) > 46129999999859/9997499999900 = 4.614153538416645696808.... The proof uses a parent-aware
  weighted certificate over continuous angle intervals and exact center-domain sweeps.
